y":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids in Le Sueur County came in under 90% of normal in November to December in 38 of 75 years since 1951, more than any other pair. In 2025 on the middle of the grids, January to February ran 19% of normal and September to October ran 55%. So far in 2026, January to February sat at 44% and June to July at 110% on the middle of the grids. Grid 28944 had its driest year in 1958 at 53% of normal.</p>"}
